oma in nude mice</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>2002</year><volume>62</volume><fpage>3711</fpage><lpage>3715</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Res||62|3711||bib18|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12097279</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grasl-Kraupp</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruttkay-Nedecky</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Koudelka</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Bukowska</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Bursch</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Schulte-Hermann</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title><italic>In situ</italic> detection of fragmented DNA (TUNEL assay) fails to discriminate among apoptosis, necrosis, and autolytic cell death: a cautionary note</article-title><source>Hepatology</source><year>1995</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>1465</fpage><lpage>1468</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Hepatology||21|1465||bib19|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7737654</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Griggs</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Metcalfe</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Hesketh</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Targeting tumour vasculature: the development of combretastatin A4</article-title><source>Lancet Oncol</source><year>2001</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>82</fpage><lpage>87</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Lancet Oncol||2|82||bib20|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11905799</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grosios</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Holwell</sur